{"term":"but","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4a8616b67bf8bf6de0","definition":"Apart from, except (for), excluding.","example":"Everyone but Father left early.","pos":"prep","synonyms":["barring","except for","save for","apart","apart from","aside","aside from","bar","barring","besides","but","but for","except","except for","excepting","excluding","forby","modulo","not counting","other than","outtake","save","save for","saving","with the exception of"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:241c36ae253269104a","definition":"Outside of.","example":"Away but the hoose and tell me whae's there.","pos":"prep","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:257d6e3cbe3329070c","definition":"Merely, only, just, no more than.","example":"Christmas comes but once a year, so we can but wait till then.","pos":"adv","synonyms":["barely","but","just","literally","merely","no more than","nothing but","only","simply"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"literary, not-comparable, poetic","register":"literary, not-comparable, poetic","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f7f3ddd7e109920a84","definition":"Though, however.","example":"I'll have to go home early but.","pos":"adv","synonyms":["even so","nevertheless","notwithstanding","yet","all that said","anyhow","all the same","be it as it may","be that as it may","but","even so","having said that","howbeit","however","just the same","maugre","natheless","nevertheless","nonetheless","notwithstanding","still","still and all","that being said","that said","though","withal","yet"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Australia, Geordie, Scotland, conjunctive, not-comparable","register":"Australia, Geordie, Scotland, conjunctive, not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b2f55b7ac5c8701e27","definition":"Used to repeat an adverb for emphasis; simply; just; absolutely.","example":"I would never, but never do such a thing!","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:148b6ddf4bf6a86e6f","definition":"However, although, nevertheless, on the other hand (introducing a clause contrary to prior belief or in contrast with the preceding clause or sentence).","example":"She is very old but still attractive.","pos":"conj","synonyms":["yet","although","ac"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:21c258e1dbee3a0a3e","definition":"On the contrary, rather (as a regular adversative conjunction, introducing a word or clause in contrast or contradiction with the preceding negative clause or sentence).","example":"I am not rich but [I am] poor.  Not John but Peter went there.","pos":"conj","synonyms":["abbur"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2fb68a84153fa64ce8","definition":"Used at the beginning of a sentence to express opposition to a remark.","example":"But I never said you could do that!","pos":"conj","synonyms":["abbur"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:22a6d854169b037f8e","definition":"Except that (introducing a subordinate clause which qualifies a negative statement); also, (archaic) with omission of the subject of the subordinate clause, acting as a negative relative, \"except one that\", \"except such that\".","example":"I cannot but feel offended.","pos":"conj","synonyms":["bar","unless","excepting","excluding","with the exception of","without"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:968b8ac0305e234817","definition":"Used to link an interjection to the following remark as an intensifier.","example":"Wow! But that's amazing!","pos":"conj","synonyms":["abbur"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:def7a85b8624e6e597","definition":"Without it also being the case that; unless that (introducing a necessary concomitant).","example":"It never rains but it pours","pos":"conj","synonyms":["abbur"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","w